  "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln\u2061u,\\,u=7-4x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7-4x}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7-4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=-1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=-1} & ={-\\frac{4}{7-4x}|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7-4(-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{11}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
